//@version=6
// ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
// │ ⚠ CORRECTION (full 2019-2026 test): THIS STRATEGY ONLY WORKED IN 2025-26 │
// │ On 7.75 years of bid/ask data it returns PF 0.98 (t -0.34). Before        │
// │ 2025-10-03 it LOSES: n=1286, WR 45.3%, PF 0.90, t -1.36. The figures      │
// │ below were validated on one year (2025-10 -> 2026-10), which turned out   │
// │ to be gold's strongest momentum regime (+65% in 2025). By year PF:        │
// │ 2019 1.05 | 2020 0.96 | 2021 0.54 | 2022 0.85 | 2023 0.93 | 2024 0.67 |   │
// │ 2025 1.44 | 2026 1.79. Do not trade it as a general-purpose strategy.     │
// │ See GOLD_BOT_README.md and gold_intraday_fade.pine for the 2019-today      │
// │ research.                                                                │
// └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  GOLD MOMENTUM SNIPER  —  XAUUSD only  —  5-minute chart
//  v2. Rebuilt from scratch after v1 failed a full-year test. See the
//  "HISTORY" note at the bottom — the previous version lost money.
//
//  THE SETUP — buy strength, hold 90 minutes, exit on the clock.
//    1. TREND      EMA50 above EMA200, and price above EMA200.
//    2. BREAKOUT   the candle CLOSES above the highest high of the prior 20.
//    3. STRONG MOMENTUM   RSI(14) above 75. This is the single most reliable
//                  signal in a year of gold tick data (+0.48 ATR expected
//                  move over the next 12 bars, t = +5.9, and it holds in BOTH
//                  halves of the year). Note it is ABOVE 75, not a 50-80
//                  band: capping RSI throws the edge away.
//    4. VOLATILITY ATR between 0.5x and 2.2x its 500-bar median.
//    Long only. No session filter — all hours tested better than any window.
//
//  THE EXIT IS TIME, NOT A TARGET.
//    Hold 18 bars (90 minutes) and close. The stop is 10x ATR and is a
//    DISASTER stop only — it fired once in 215 trades.
//    This is the whole point of the rebuild. The signal predicts a small
//    drift (~0.5 ATR), and a tight stop sits well inside the noise around
//    that drift, so a normal stop-and-target scalp gets stopped out by
//    randomness before the edge can show up. Removing the tight stop and
//    exiting on the clock is what turned a losing strategy into a working
//    one. Do not "improve" this by tightening the stop.
//
//  ── VERIFIED (93.0M real Dukascopy ticks, 2025-10-03 → 2026-10-02) ────────
//    215 trades | Win rate 53.0% | Profit factor 1.52
//    (set Minimum RSI to 80 for 55.9% WR / PF 1.87 on 102 trades — better on
//     both metrics, but half the sample; 75 ships as the better-estimated one)
//    Max drawdown 3.35R | avg win +0.289R, avg loss -0.214R
//    t-statistic +2.19 | bootstrap P(not profitable) 1.3%
//    95% CI on mean R per trade [+0.006, +0.100] — excludes zero
//    8 of 13 months profitable | average hold 1h29m
//  Spread paid on entry AND exit; stop-vs-exit resolved on the real tick
//  sequence, not on bar OHLC.
//
//  ── WHY THIS DOES NOT REPAINT ─────────────────────────────────────────────
//  * calc_on_every_tick = false  -> evaluated only at BAR CLOSE.
//  * The broken range is ta.highest(high, 20)[1] — the bars BEFORE the signal
//    bar. That [1] offset is what stops a level being redrawn by the very bar
//    being judged.
//  * process_orders_on_close = false -> fills at the NEXT bar's OPEN.
//  * Entry / Stop / Time-exit are drawn only AFTER the signal bar closes and
//    are pinned to fixed prices and a fixed bar. Once printed they never move.
//  * No request.security(), no lookahead, no future-referencing functions.
//
//  ── HONEST LIMITS — read before risking money ─────────────────────────────
//  * MARGINAL SIGNIFICANCE. t = +2.19 is just past the usual threshold, and
//    this config was picked from ~24 tested. What makes it credible is that
//    the WHOLE RSI>75 family scored PF 1.45-1.57 (t 1.86-2.28) across every
//    horizon and stop width tried — a flat, broad plateau rather than one
//    lucky cell. But it is not proof.
//  * CONCENTRATED. January 2026 alone produced +5.2R of the +11.3R total.
//    5 of 13 months lost money. Expect flat or negative stretches.
//  * LONG ONLY, AND THAT IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT. Every bearish signal tested
//    flipped sign between the two halves of the year. Gold trended up over
//    this period; this strategy has a bull-market tailwind baked in and has
//    NOT been shown to work in a gold downtrend.
//  * POSITION SIZING. With a 10x ATR stop (~$45 on gold), 1R is large. Risk a
//    fixed % of equity on that distance — do NOT size as if it were a scalp
//    stop, or one disaster stop will hurt badly.
//  * ONE YEAR, ONE INSTRUMENT, 215 trades. Forward-test on demo first.
//
//  ── HOW TO USE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  1. Open XAUUSD (gold) on the 5-minute timeframe.
//  2. Add this script, then open the "Strategy Tester" tab.
//  3. Properties -> Slippage: about HALF your broker's typical gold spread in
//     ticks (spread ~0.40, mintick 0.01 => ~20). Charged per side, so half
//     each side equals one full spread per round turn. At zero slippage the
//     tester will flatter these numbers.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
strategy("Gold Momentum Sniper (XAUUSD M5)",
     overlay                 = true,
     initial_capital         = 10000,
     currency                = currency.USD,
     default_qty_type        = strategy.fixed,
     default_qty_value       = 1,
     calc_on_every_tick      = false,
     process_orders_on_close = false,
     max_labels_count        = 500,
     max_lines_count         = 500,
     max_boxes_count         = 500)

// ─────────────────────────────── Inputs ───────────────────────────────────
gS = "1 · Signal"
boLen    = input.int(20, "Breakout range length (bars)", minval=3, group=gS,
     tooltip="The close must break the highest high of this many PRIOR bars.")
emaFast  = input.int(50,  "Fast EMA", minval=5,  group=gS)
emaSlow  = input.int(200, "Trend EMA", minval=20, group=gS)
useStack = input.bool(true, "Require EMA50 above EMA200", group=gS)
rsiLen   = input.int(14, "RSI length", minval=2, group=gS)
rsiMin   = input.float(75, "Minimum RSI (buy strength)", step=1, group=gS,
     tooltip="ABOVE this, with no upper cap — capping RSI discards the strongest signal in the data. Measured on a full year with this exact exit: RSI>65 PF 1.01, RSI>70 PF 1.20 (389 trades), RSI>75 PF 1.52 (215), RSI>80 PF 1.87 (102). Raising it to 80 gives the best win rate AND profit factor but only ~2 trades a week.")

gV = "2 · Volatility regime"
atrLen    = input.int(14,  "ATR length", minval=2, group=gV)
atrMedLen = input.int(500, "ATR median lookback", minval=50, group=gV)
atrMin    = input.float(0.5, "Skip if ATR / median below", step=0.05, group=gV)
atrMax    = input.float(2.2, "Skip if ATR / median above", step=0.05, group=gV)

gR = "3 · Risk and exit"
holdBars = input.int(18, "Hold for N bars, then close", minval=2, group=gR,
     tooltip="18 bars = 90 minutes on M5. THIS is the exit. Tested 6/12/18/24/30/36; 18-36 all work, 6 does not.")
slAtr    = input.float(10.0, "Disaster stop (x ATR)", step=0.5, minval=1.0, group=gR,
     tooltip="Deliberately far away. It fired once in 215 trades. Tightening it is what made the previous version lose money.")
coolBars = input.int(3, "Cooldown bars after an exit", minval=0, group=gR)

gD = "4 · Display"
showLines = input.bool(true, "Draw Entry / Stop / Time-exit", group=gD)
showLbl   = input.bool(true, "Show price labels", group=gD)
showRef   = input.bool(true, "Show +1 / +2 ATR reference levels", group=gD,
     tooltip="Reference only. The strategy does NOT exit at these — it exits on the clock.")
showPanel = input.bool(true, "Show performance panel", group=gD)

// ───────────────────── Indicators (closed bars only) ──────────────────────
atrV   = ta.atr(atrLen)
atrMed = ta.median(atrV, atrMedLen)
rsiV   = ta.rsi(close, rsiLen)
emaF   = ta.ema(close, emaFast)
emaS   = ta.ema(close, emaSlow)

// The range being broken: extremes of the bars BEFORE this one.
boHi = ta.highest(high, boLen)[1]

volOK   = not na(atrMed) and atrV >= atrMin * atrMed and atrV <= atrMax * atrMed
trendOK = close > emaS and (not useStack or emaF > emaS)
baseOK  = volOK and not na(emaS) and not na(boHi) and not na(atrV)

longSig = baseOK and trendOK and close > boHi and rsiV > rsiMin

// ───────────────────────────── Trade state ────────────────────────────────
var int   lastExitBar = -100000
var float curStop     = na
var int   entryBar    = na

flat     = strategy.position_size == 0
canTrade = flat and (bar_index - lastExitBar) > coolBars

if longSig and canTrade
    strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long)

justOpened = strategy.position_size > 0 and strategy.position_size[1] == 0

var line  lnE = na
var line  lnS = na
var line  lnT = na
var line  lnR1 = na
var line  lnR2 = na
var label lbE = na
var label lbS = na
var label lbT = na

// ────────── Levels are pinned at the fill, then never change ──────────────
if justOpened
    e = strategy.position_avg_price
    // atrV[1] is the SIGNAL bar's ATR: the signal closed last bar and we
    // filled on this bar's open. Using atrV here would use a bar the signal
    // never saw.
    a = atrV[1]
    if not na(a) and a > 0
        curStop  := e - slAtr * a
        entryBar := bar_index
        exitBar  = bar_index + holdBars

        if showLines
            lnE := line.new(bar_index, e, exitBar, e, color=color.new(color.blue, 0), width=2)
            lnS := line.new(bar_index, curStop, exitBar, curStop, color=color.new(color.red, 0), width=2, style=line.style_dashed)
            lnT := line.new(exitBar, curStop, exitBar, e + 2 * a, color=color.new(color.gray, 30), width=1, style=line.style_dotted)
        if showRef
            lnR1 := line.new(bar_index, e + a,     exitBar, e + a,     color=color.new(color.teal, 40), width=1, style=line.style_dotted)
            lnR2 := line.new(bar_index, e + 2 * a, exitBar, e + 2 * a, color=color.new(color.teal, 60), width=1, style=line.style_dotted)
        if showLbl
            lbE := label.new(bar_index, e, text=str.tostring(e, format.mintick) + "  ENTRY LONG",
                 style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(color.blue, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
            lbS := label.new(bar_index, curStop, text=str.tostring(curStop, format.mintick) + "  DISASTER STOP (-1R)",
                 style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(color.red, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
            lbT := label.new(exitBar, e + 2 * a, text="TIME EXIT in " + str.tostring(holdBars) + " bars",
                 style=label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.gray, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)

inTrade = strategy.position_size > 0 and not na(curStop)

if inTrade
    strategy.exit("Stop", from_entry="Long", stop=curStop, comment_loss="DISASTER SL")
    if bar_index - entryBar >= holdBars
        strategy.close("Long", comment="TIME EXIT")

// Everything freezes on the exit bar: a permanent, non-repainting record.
if flat and not flat[1]
    lastExitBar := bar_index
    curStop     := na

// ─────────────────────────── Signal markers ───────────────────────────────
plotshape(longSig and canTrade, title="Momentum breakout", style=shape.triangleup,
     location=location.belowbar, color=color.new(color.green, 0), size=size.tiny)
plot(emaS, "Trend EMA 200", color=color.new(color.orange, 40), linewidth=1)
plot(emaF, "Fast EMA 50",   color=color.new(color.aqua, 60), linewidth=1)

// ───────────────────────── Performance panel ──────────────────────────────
if showPanel and barstate.islast
    tot  = strategy.closedtrades
    wins = strategy.wintrades
    wr   = tot > 0 ? 100.0 * wins / tot : 0.0
    pf   = strategy.grossloss > 0 ? strategy.grossprofit / strategy.grossloss : 0.0
    var table p = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 5, border_width=1)
    table.cell(p, 0, 0, "GOLD MOMENTUM", bgcolor=color.new(color.blue, 0), text_color=color.white, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(p, 1, 0, "XAUUSD M5",     bgcolor=color.new(color.blue, 0), text_color=color.white, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(p, 0, 1, "Trades",        text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(p, 1, 1, str.tostring(tot), text_color=color.white, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(p, 0, 2, "Win rate",      text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(p, 1, 2, str.tostring(wr, "#.##") + " %",
         text_color = wr >= 50 ? color.lime : wr >= 45 ? color.orange : color.red, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(p, 0, 3, "Profit factor", text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(p, 1, 3, str.tostring(pf, "#.##"),
         text_color = pf >= 1.4 ? color.lime : pf >= 1.0 ? color.orange : color.red, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(p, 0, 4, "Net P&L",       text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(p, 1, 4, str.tostring(strategy.netprofit, "#.##"),
         text_color = strategy.netprofit >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red, text_size=size.small)

// ──────────────────────────────── Alerts ──────────────────────────────────
alertcondition(longSig, title="Gold Momentum LONG",
     message="Gold Momentum Sniper: LONG breakout, RSI>75, on XAUUSD M5")

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  HISTORY — what v1 got wrong, measured rather than guessed
//  v1 was a 20-bar breakout with RSI banded 50-80, a 1.8x ATR stop, a 1.5R
//  target and a 12:00-20:00 UTC session filter. On 90 days it showed 49.2% WR
//  and PF 1.42. On a FULL YEAR of ticks the same config returned PF 0.92 and
//  -28R, with a 64.8R drawdown; across the 9 months it had never seen, PF
//  0.80. Everything that looked good was a regime artifact:
//    - the session window helped on 90 days and HURT over the year
//    - the long/short split inverted between the two samples
//    - the RSI 50-80 band excluded RSI>75, the one signal that held up
//  Also measured and rejected, with numbers:
//    - retest entries (PF 1.42 -> 0.97): breakouts that come back to the
//      level are the FAILING ones; the good ones never fill you
//    - breakeven stops (WR 49% -> 31%)
//    - a 0.5R target: 61.6% win rate, PF 0.82 — loses in BOTH halves. A high
//      win rate is not an edge.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
